<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lower Dir District</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lower Dir is a district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-west-frontier-province">Khyber Pakhtunkhwa</a> province in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, with its headquarters at Timergara. It was formed in 1996, when Dir District, created from the princely state of Dir after its abolition in 1969, was divided into Upper and Lower Dir. It lies in the Panjkora valley and is inhabited mainly by Yusufzai <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pashtuns">Pashtuns</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lower-dir-district.jpg" alt="Lower Dir District" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kalival · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Viw_of_Timergara_in_Summer._JPG.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
